        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: begründen",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "begründen — \"to give reasons for, to justify; to found\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Der Lehrer hat seine Entscheidung gut begründet. The teacher gave good reasons for his decision."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Etwas begründen — to back it up with reasons. It also means to found: eine Schule begründen."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "begründen is inherited from Middle High German begründen \"to found, to make solid\" (EtymDB), built on Grund \"ground, reason\", from Proto-Germanic grunduz \"ground\": you put ground under your words."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for telling, explaining and describing at B1."
